Optional PC comparisons use Ultralytics YOLOv5n/s v7.0 ONNX weights, GPL-3.0.
Source: https://github.com/ultralytics/yolov5/releases/tag/v7.0
See LICENSE-YOLOv5. URLs and file hashes: tools/fetch-video-model.py.
YOLO11n comparison: Ultralytics weights converted to ONNX by webnn/yolo11n,
pinned Hugging Face revision in tools/fetch-video-model.py; AGPL-3.0.
See LICENSE-YOLO11 and https://huggingface.co/webnn/yolo11n.
The PC ONNX adapter uses RGB/255 letterboxing, decoded xywh boxes and NMS;
the v5 score is objectness times class score; YOLO11 has no objectness column.
YOLOv5n also has a native Raspberry Pi adapter in src/yolov5.hpp.
Its NCNN export retains the exact studied v7.0 weights, promotes stored FP16
constants to FP32, and lowers SiLU to x * sigmoid(x). Export procedure and
source/artifact hashes: tools/export-yolov5-ncnn.py and models/yolov5n-ncnn.json.
Other comparison candidates have not been deployed to the Raspberry Pi.

